  "handoffMarkdown": "RPZ-2 local preview, release-plz 0.3.172 (latest; built with Rust 1.99.0 outside the repo because its deps need rustc >= 1.97). Scratch clone artifacts-temp/agentx/signalr-releases/scratch with this release-plz.toml, version 1.0.0, configured header + `## [1.0.0]`, tagged v1.0.0 locally, origin URL set but never pushed; `release-plz update --config release-plz.toml`, `git reset --hard v1.0.0` between cases; logs in artifacts-temp/agentx/signalr-releases/rpz-logs/. (1) config accepted, pr_branch_prefix included, no unknown-key warning (only \"no upstream\" warnings). Note: commits must touch package files (empty commits are ignored by release-plz). (2) docs: x, docs(agentx): x, test(e2e): x -> \"no commit matches the release_commits regex\", no file changed. (3) docs: y, docs(agentx): q, fix(client): x -> 1.0.1; `## [1.0.1] - <date>` inserted between the single header and `## [1.0.0]`; Documentation \"- y\" listed, docs(agentx) absent; Fixes \"- *(client)* x\". (4a) feat(client): x -> 1.1.0. (4b) fix(client): y + feat(client) whose body states a removed builder option and ends with `Migration: call ...` + docs: z -> 1.1.0; Features line followed by indented \"  - Migration: call `with_handshake_timeout` instead of `with_timeout`.\". (5) fix(client) removing `pub use communication::cookies::CookieJar` from src/lib.rs -> 1.0.1 (no semver check run). (6) Cargo.lock absent at start and git-ignored: release-plz succeeds, creates an ignored Cargo.lock, `git status --porcelain` lists only Cargo.toml and CHANGELOG.md, so Cargo.lock stays ignored. Changelog dates are UTC (release-plz timestamp).",
